  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A circle passing through the point&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>&#946;</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> in the first quadrant touches the two coordinate axes at the points&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mo>.</mo></math> The point&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math>&nbsp;is above the line&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mo>.</mo></math> The point&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi></math>&nbsp;on the line segment&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;is the foot of perpendicular from&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math>&nbsp;on&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;If&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi></math>&nbsp;is equal to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>11</mn></math> units, then the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi><mi>&#946;</mi></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi></math></p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "121",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Let the equation of circle touching both the coordinate axis be,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>r</mi><msup><mo>)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>r</mi><msup><mo>)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;which&nbsp;passes through&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>&#946;</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>So,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>r</mi><msup><mo>)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>r</mi><msup><mo>)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>Also equation of line&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mo>:</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>r</mi></math></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/744d7ab7-d7e1-438e-b442-2d90dd9a532e-image.png\" style=\"width: 200px; height: 166px;\" /></p><p>Let&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>,</p><p>Now using the formula of foot of perpendicular,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>&#945;</mi></mrow><mn>1</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>&#946;</mi></mrow><mn>1</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mi>&#945;</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mi>&#946;</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mi>&#945;</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mi>&#946;</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Now using the distance formula we get,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>121</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>-</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>)</mo><msup><mo>)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>242</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>&#946;</mi><msup><mo>)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>r</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>242</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi>&#945;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>&#946;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>&#945;</mi><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>r</mi><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>r</mi><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>242</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>&#945;</mi><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>242</mn></math>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"}\" open=\"{\"><mrow><mtext>from&#160;equation</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>r</mi><msup><mo>)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>r</mi><msup><mo>)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>121</mn></math></p></blockquote>",
